    "operator": "Replace the requirement that BOTH Alice and Bob like at least k chosen books by EITHER Alice OR Bob liking at least k chosen books (inclusive OR). Minimize the same total reading time.",
    "correctness_argument": "Positive costs exclude unused books. For each count j<=k of books liked by both readers, the minimum completion uses the cheapest max(0,k-j) Alice-only and Bob-only books. Prefix sums over the three sorted groups enumerate all possibilities. The L3 inclusive-OR optimum is the cheaper of the k cheapest Alice-liked books and k cheapest Bob-liked books. The oracle enumerates every subset and checks the stated predicates.",
